{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for getting in touch. Your account is active and not locked. It's still waiting for you to set your own password, so your temporary password is still accepted. The error most likely means the new password you picked doesn't meet our rules. Please try this:\n\n1. Change it on your laptop's Windows sign-in screen, not a web page. Make sure you're in the office or connected to VPN.\n2. Make your new password at least 14 characters long. A short phrase works well, for example three or four words with a number. It can't be a password you've used recently.\n3. Check that Caps Lock is off and the keyboard language is right. When typing the temporary password, watch for look-alike characters like l and I, or 0 and O.\n\nIf it still fails, please reply with the exact error message (a screenshot is ideal) and tell us whether you were on the Windows sign-in screen or a web page. We'll take it from there. If the temporary password itself stops working, we can set up a new one and give it to you by phone.",
  "internal_note": "KB-003 checks: lookup_user (id 12). Status active, must_change_password=true, failed_login_count=0, not blocked, VPN enabled. password_last_set 2026-10-09 14:20 UTC, so a temporary password was recently issued. Sign-in logs: 9 successful sign-ins, all from New York on corporate or residential networks during usual hours. 0 failed passwords, no hosting networks, nothing suspicious. Laptop BL-LT-0112 is online with no warnings. Most likely cause: the new password breaks policy (under 14 characters or a reused password), or the change is being tried on a web page instead of the Windows sign-in screen. No unlock needed, and no reset requested since the temporary password still appears valid. Gave the user KB-003 fix steps and asked for the exact error text and where they're signing in. Next steps if it still fails: check for lockout and unlock (KB-003 step 3), or issue a new temporary password per KB-002, delivered by phone. Escalate if the account is active with no change required and still no password works.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-003",
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
